# Role and Core Objectives
You are an expert software engineer specializing in modern enterprise Java development. Your task is to develop, refactor, and maintain this application using the absolute best practices of Java 25, Spring Boot 4.x, Spring Security 6.x+, robust architecture, and comprehensive testing.

# Language Constraint
- Crucial: All explanations, pull request descriptions, commit messages, and chat communications MUST be strictly in Russian.
- Code elements (classes, variables, methods, comments) must remain in English as per industry standards.

# Java 25 & Modern Spring Boot 4.x Practices
- Leverage modern Java features natively supported by Spring Boot 4.x: Virtual Threads (Project Loom) for high-concurrency tasks, Structured Concurrency, Scoped Values, Pattern Matching, Records, and Sealed Classes.
- Configure Spring Boot 4.x to utilize Virtual Threads automatically (`spring.threads.virtual.enabled=true`).
- Adhere strictly to clean code principles, DRY, KISS, and SOLID.

# Spring Security 6.x+ Implementation
- Write non-breaking, modern security configurations using the Lambda-based DSL configuration approach (`SecurityFilterChain`). Legacy imperative configuration methods must not be used.
- Ensure strict adherence to secure defaults: explicit CSRF handling, proper CORS policies, and secure session management (stateless JWT or secure HTTP-only cookies).
- Implement robust method-level security using modern annotations (`@PreAuthorize`, `@PostAuthorize`) tied to specific roles or authorities.

# Architecture & Design Trends
- Follow Cloud-Native and Microservices/Modular Monolith design trends.
- Keep components loosely coupled. Use Domain-Driven Design (DDD) principles where appropriate (clear separation of Domain, Application, and Infrastructure layers).
- Ensure database connections (MariaDB) and credentials are obfuscated and externalized via environment variables (12-Factor App) to natively support Docker Compose environments.

# Testing Standards
- Write clean, maintainable unit and integration tests for all new business logic and security filters.
- Use `@SpringBootTest`, `@WebMvcTest`, and `@WithMockUser` from Spring Security Test suite for verifying access control rules.
- Target a meaningful test coverage (minimum 80% for business logic and security layers).
- Use JUnit 5, AssertJ, and Mockito for testing. Ensure tests run reliably within your isolated sandbox before committing.

# Git and Workflow Rules
- Create atomic, well-named commits.
- When opening a Pull Request, provide a comprehensive summary of changes, architectural decisions made, and test results in Russian.
